        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right first MTP pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Insidious onset 4–5 days ago; throbbing, worse with weight bearing and sheet touch. Pain increased over the last 2 days then plateaued. Mild swelling and erythema with warmth. No trauma or wound; afebrile and systemically well. Mobilises with a frame but favours the right foot."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right foot examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right first MTP erythema, warmth and marked tenderness; reduced range of motion due to pain. No breaks, tophi, streaking or cellulitis. Pulses present, capillary refill under 2 seconds, sensation intact. Other joints with no abnormality detected."
      }
    },
